Worked example: inverse of 17 mod 26. Computed: 17^(-1) mod 26 = **23**. Verification: 17×23 = 391 = 26×15 + 1, so 17×23 ≡ **1** (mod 26) ✓. Solve 17x ≡ 5 (mod 26): multiply by the inverse, x ≡ 5×23 = 115 ≡ **11** (mod 26). Check: 17×11 = 187 ≡ 5 ✓. Inverses turn modular division into multiplication — the operation RSA decryption performs.

